# player-subtick-corpus.manifest - rows of tests/harness/check_player_subtick.sh.
#   <bk2> | <lo>-<hi>[,<lo>-<hi>...]
#   bk2    a movie under games/spyro-2/bk2
#   span   a range of intermediate-present VBLs, two apart; every VBL of it
#          but the first is a leg, compared with the capture two VBLs earlier
# Ice skating: the body advances one keyframe per four ticks with long head
# travel; the advances fall on legs 1494, 1502, 1694, 1702 and 1734. The
# reflective ice draws the mirrored copy, measured as its own series.
colossus-ice-skating.bk2 | 1486-1504,1686-1704,1726-1740
# Walking and a portal entry: a keyframe advance nearly every tick at short
# head travel.
autumn-plains-skelos-badlands-portal-entry.bk2 | 1524-1650
# The same movie across the regime edge at engine VBL 1139 (capture VBL
# 1712), where the portal fly-in hands over to the load with the camera
# static: the camera rule does not cut there, so the player is interpolated
# through the edge. A run captures at most 64 presents, so the span is its
# own row.
autumn-plains-skelos-badlands-portal-entry.bk2 | 1700-1724
